# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

On a phone, held upright or on its side (everywhere the roomy query `(min-width: 761px) and (min-height: 501px)` does not match), a DEF unit is drawn as large as its unit zone's inside allows. Its turned footprint fills the zone's width or its height, whichever runs out first, never overflows either, and is never bigger than the card's own size. `--def-scale` is computed from the lane's width and the row's height instead of the constant 0.72. Desktop and tablet behaviour from #2347 stays exactly as it is, and `positionSwitched` still ends on the resting transform, because `Card.tsx` and `animations.css` keep the string `rotate(90deg) scale(var(--def-scale, 1))`. `board-layout.cy.tsx` measures the footprint at 360x780, 390x844, 430x932 and three landscape phones. The unit test that pins 0.72 is updated.

## Files to touch

| Path | new/change | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/board.css` | change | Base `.lane` rule (about lines 883–896): its comment, three custom properties replacing `--def-scale: 0.72`, and `container-type: inline-size`. Roomy `.lane` rule (about lines 912–920): add `container-type: normal` and a comment |
| `apps/web/src/game/position-switch.test.tsx` | change | The `#2330` describe's one `it`: pin the formula and the containment instead of `0.72` |
| `e2e/cypress/component/board-layout.cy.tsx` | change | `#2330` describe: four more non-roomy sizes, an `insideOf` helper, the phone footprint checks, and a `layout:report` row per DEF card |

Do not touch: `apps/web/src/game/Card.tsx` and `apps/web/src/game/animations.css`. Their DEF transform string is pinned by `position-switch.test.tsx`, `Card.test.tsx:336` (M5-T4) and `__snapshots__/Board.test.tsx.snap`, and it stays as it is. Also leave alone `docs/polish/6-cards.md`, anything in `crates/`, `spec/`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `bot/`, every `package.json` and every lockfile. No ruling and no spec section governs this: it is client layout, not a rules decision, so no R number and no pending fragment. The constraints that bind are BUILD M5-T1 (the board fits), M5-T4 (the inline `rotate(90deg)`), B29 (the 44 px touch floor) and CLAUDE.md rule 7, which this change leaves alone.

